From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Silets <joshuasilets@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 20:04:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat: expose WebAuthn hybrid transport via
 'webauthn-hybrid-request'

Chromium adds the hybrid (caBLE v2) transport to every WebAuthn request,
but only creates the discovery once the embedder configures a QR
generator key in ConfigureDiscoveries. Electron never did, so a request
that a site expected to serve over hybrid transport sat forever with no
UI and no error.

Override ConfigureDiscoveries to generate the key, emit a new session
event 'webauthn-hybrid-request' carrying the FIDO:/ QR payload for the
app to render, and configure the discovery only when a listener accepted
the event. Store the Bluetooth callbacks so the OS permission prompt is
requested once the transport enumeration reports it pending. Emit
'webauthn-hybrid-request-completed' when the request ends so the app can
dismiss its QR code.

Requests with conditional or passkey-upgrade UI presentation are
skipped, as are platforms where Chromium would not create the discovery
(no BLE support, or Windows 11 which implements hybrid natively).

Assisted-By: Claude Fable 5.1, Claude Code

[Rebased onto collect-webauthn-pin: reuse the delegate's GetSession(),
RequestTypeName() returns std::string_view for current gin, specs ported
from mocha/chai to vitest; the hybrid specs enable the virtual
authenticator UI and pick an account for discoverable get().
With a lone PIN-protected security key, Chromium asks for its PIN
without waiting for a touch, which binds the request to that key, so a
phone scanning the QR code could never connect. Added: answering
'collect-webauthn-pin' with { useAnotherDevice: true } starts the
request over, like Chrome's "use another device", reusing the QR key so
the code stays valid and holding the Bluetooth adapter across the restart
so BlueZ does not refuse the new scan while the old one stops.
Dropped turning Bluetooth on automatically when it is off: without UI to
ask, that is the user's decision; the docs say it must be on.
-- Oleksandr Kulkov]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
